      <p>Where X<sub>n,it</sub> is the value of predictor n for sound event t in participant i, β<sub>n</sub> is its coefficient, and β<sub>0i</sub> is the participant-specific intercept.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Generating a Decision Rule</h2>
      <p>I fit a regularized logistic model that predicts the probability that an Fz estimate falls within 45° of the reference, using different combinations of predictor variables, each combination constituting a different decision rule. At a low threshold, the decision rule accepts many opportunities but includes more errors, and at a high threshold, the decision rule improves accuracy with the consequence of forgoing high coverage. I trace this tradeoff by plotting the proportion of target agreement with respect to multichannel data against coverage. I compare different gated models to the ungated Fz model and to each other, designating which model forgoes the least coverage while maximizing accuracy.</p>
    </section>

